<title>UK: ICCO details result of cocoa buffer stock sale.</title>
<headline>ICCO details result of cocoa buffer stock sale.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The International Cocoa Organization (ICCO) said the 4,250 tonne buffer-stock sale earlier on Friday was completed at the following prices.</p>
<p> ORIGIN	TONNES QUALITY  CROP YEAR   PORT    US DLR</p>
<p>PRICE/TONNE</p>
<p>Cameroon	  49    GF	1981/82  Rotterdam   $1,264</p>
<p>Cote d'Ivoire  224    GF	1981/82  Amsterdam   $1,376-1,392</p>
<p>Cote d'Ivoire  320    FF	1981/82  Amsterdam   $1,325</p>
<p>Cote d'Ivoire  765    GF	1981/82  Rotterdam   $1,376-1,389</p>
<p>Cote d'Ivoire  275    FF	1981/82  Rotterdam   $1,325</p>
<p>Ghana	    690    GF	1986/87  Rotterdam   $1,435-1,440</p>
<p>Ghana	    294    FF	1986/87  Rotterdam   $1,390</p>
<p>Ghana	     48    GF	1987/88  Rotterdam   $1,440</p>
<p>Ghana	    100    FF	1987/88  Rotterdam   $1,390</p>
<p>Nigeria	   99    GF	1980/81  Rotterdam   $1,365</p>
<p>Nigeria	  241    FF	1980/81  Rotterdam   $1,325</p>
<p>Nigeria	  148    GF	1986/87  Rotterdam   $1,380</p>
<p>Nigeria	  322    FF	1986/87  Rotterdam   $1,325</p>
<p>Togo		94    GF	1987/88  Rotterdam   $1,380</p>
<p>Bahia	    478  As seen   1987/88  Antwerp     $1,152-1,260</p>
<p>Ghana	     29  As seen   1981/82  Antwerp     $1,160-1,260</p>
<p>Nigeria	   65  As seen   1980/81  Antwerp     $1,130-1,260</p>
<p>Nigeria	   10  As seen   1986/87  Antwerp     $1,130-1,260</p>
<p>(GF=good fermented, FF=fair fermented)</p>
<p>The ICCO said the carry for forward delivery was calculated at $12 per tonne per month.</p>
<p>-- Clelia Oziel, London Newsroom 044 71 542 8072.</p>
